{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And He placed there the human.</b> But at the time of his creation he was not from there, for had he been created in Eden and his standing there, he would have supposed that the entire world is like that. Rather, He created him outside, and he saw the whole world full of thorns and thistles, and afterward He brought him into Eden, a choice place." "<b>And He planted.</b> Meaning he had already planted — and so too 'and caused to sprout,' for the plants existed before the human. Said R. Shmuel ben Nahmani: you might think before the creation of the world — rather, before the creation of the human. And as for what we say that it is among the things that preceded the world, that refers to the Eden. But the trees He planted on the third day."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:02:25.167426597Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}